{"title":"Career Roadmap — Product Designer","role":"Product Designer","summary":"A Product Designer creates physical products by combining user needs, functionality, materials, manufacturing, aesthetics, ergonomics and commercial requirements.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Des (Bachelor of Design)","Course":"Ceramic & Glass Design"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Product Designer creates physical products by combining user needs, functionality, materials, manufacturing, aesthetics, ergonomics and commercial requirements."},{"type":"p","text":"For a student specialising in Ceramic & Glass Design, the strongest product-design profile combines traditional material expertise with broader industrial/product design capabilities."},{"type":"p","text":"Potential product areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Tableware"},{"text":"Kitchenware"},{"text":"Home décor"},{"text":"Lighting"},{"text":"Furniture components"},{"text":"Bathroom products"},{"text":"Consumer products"},{"text":"Glassware"},{"text":"Ceramic products"},{"text":"Lifestyle products"},{"text":"Sustainable products"},{"text":"Packaging"},{"text":"Architectural objects"},{"text":"Premium/luxury products"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The student should avoid becoming limited to only handcrafted ceramic objects. The goal is to develop the ability to research a problem, design a product, prototype it, understand manufacturing and take it toward production."},{"type":"h","text":"Typical Route"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des Ceramic & Glass Design","Product Design + Material Specialisation","Product Design Internship","Junior Product Designer","Product Designer","Senior Product Designer","Lead Product Designer","Design Manager / Design Director"]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Design fundamentals + material exploration"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Product development + ceramics/glass"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Industrial design + manufacturing"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Professional product design + portfolio"}],[{"text":"0–2 years"},{"text":"Junior Product Designer"}],[{"text":"2–5 years"},{"text":"Product Designer"}],[{"text":"5–8 years"},{"text":"Senior Product Designer"}],[{"text":"8+ years"},{"text":"Lead / Design Manager / Design Director"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Design Fundamentals & Materials"},{"type":"p","text":"The first year should establish strong design fundamentals."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design principles"},{"text":"Form and proportion"},{"text":"Colour theory"},{"text":"Composition"},{"text":"Sketching"},{"text":"Perspective"},{"text":"Visualisation"},{"text":"Design history"},{"text":"Ergonomics"},{"text":"Basic model-making"},{"text":"Material exploration"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Ceramic Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clay types"},{"text":"Clay preparation"},{"text":"Hand-building"},{"text":"Wheel throwing"},{"text":"Moulding"},{"text":"Slip casting"},{"text":"Glazing"},{"text":"Firing"},{"text":"Surface finishing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Glass Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Explore:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hot glass"},{"text":"Cold working"},{"text":"Glass cutting"},{"text":"Fusing"},{"text":"Slumping"},{"text":"Moulding"},{"text":"Surface treatment"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year-1 Project"},{"type":"h","text":"Functional Tableware Collection"},{"type":"p","text":"Design:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cup"},{"text":"Plate"},{"text":"Bowl"},{"text":"Serving vessel"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Document:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research","Sketches","Form Exploration","Material Experiments","Prototype","Testing","Final Product"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Product Development"},{"type":"p","text":"Year 2 should move from artistic exploration toward functional product design."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"User research"},{"text":"Product ergonomics"},{"text":"Human dimensions"},{"text":"Product form development"},{"text":"Design specifications"},{"text":"Material selection"},{"text":"Prototyping"},{"text":"Model-making"},{"text":"Product photography"},{"text":"Basic manufacturing processes"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Study Product Categories"},{"type":"p","text":"Explore:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Kitchen products"},{"text":"Home accessories"},{"text":"Lighting"},{"text":"Furniture"},{"text":"Bathroom products"},{"text":"Lifestyle products"},{"text":"Consumer goods"},{"text":"Hospitality products"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Product Development Process"},{"type":"flow","items":["User Problem","Research","Opportunity","Concepts","Sketches","Material Selection","Prototype","Testing","Refinement","Final Product"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year-2 Project"},{"type":"h","text":"Sustainable Kitchen Product"},{"type":"p","text":"For example:"},{"type":"p","text":"A modular ceramic food-storage system."},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"User requirements"},{"text":"Stackability"},{"text":"Storage"},{"text":"Cleaning"},{"text":"Manufacturing"},{"text":"Material efficiency"},{"text":"Packaging"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Industrial Product Design & Manufacturing"},{"type":"p","text":"Year 3 should expand beyond ceramic and glass into broader product-development skills."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn Manufacturing"},{"type":"h","text":"Ceramics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Slip casting"},{"text":"Press moulding"},{"text":"Jiggering"},{"text":"Industrial glazing"},{"text":"Kiln processes"},{"text":"Production tolerances"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Glass"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Moulding"},{"text":"Pressed glass"},{"text":"Blown glass"},{"text":"Fusing"},{"text":"Tempering"},{"text":"Finishing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Other Materials"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the basics of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Wood"},{"text":"Metal"},{"text":"Plastic"},{"text":"Silicone"},{"text":"Textiles"},{"text":"Composites"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A product designer needs to know when ceramic/glass is appropriate and when another material is better."}]},{"heading":"CAD & 3D Modelling","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop proficiency in at least one professional 3D workflow."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Rhino"},{"text":"SolidWorks"},{"text":"Fusion 360"},{"text":"Autodesk Alias"},{"text":"Blender"},{"text":"KeyShot"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For ceramic/glass product design, a strong combination is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Rhino","KeyShot","Adobe Illustrator/Photoshop"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"For engineering-heavy product development:"},{"type":"h","text":"SolidWorks/Fusion 360 + KeyShot"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"3D modelling"},{"text":"Surface modelling"},{"text":"Parametric modelling"},{"text":"Product assemblies"},{"text":"Technical drawings"},{"text":"Dimensions"},{"text":"Tolerances"},{"text":"Manufacturing documentation"},{"text":"Rendering"}]}]},{"heading":"Year 4 — Professional Product Design","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Year 4 should demonstrate the ability to take a product from problem to production-ready concept."},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced Areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design strategy"},{"text":"Product architecture"},{"text":"Manufacturing feasibility"},{"text":"Cost awareness"},{"text":"Material optimisation"},{"text":"Sustainable design"},{"text":"Design for manufacturing"},{"text":"Design for assembly"},{"text":"Packaging"},{"text":"Brand identity"},{"text":"Product launch"},{"text":"User testing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Final-Year Project"},{"type":"p","text":"A strong project could be:"},{"type":